{"case_id":"T8025","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","input_semantics","configuration"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["simdjson::internal::allocate_padded_buffer(size_t)"],"reason":"H0 does not directly fuzz the changed allocator with independently generated size_t lengths, so it misses the new arithmetic-overflow boundary and the FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION allocation-limit branch. Parser-mediated calls derive allocation lengths from physically supplied fuzz inputs and therefore cannot practically cover values near SIZE_MAX that make length + SIMDJSON_PADDING wrap.","evidence":["S1 adds `if(totalpaddedlength<length) return nullptr;` in `allocate_padded_buffer(size_t length)`, creating boundary semantics at lengths near `SIZE_MAX`.","S1 adds a `FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION` branch rejecting `totalpaddedlength>(1UL<<20)`, making large synthetic length values safely fuzzable.","No H0 target calls `simdjson::internal::allocate_padded_buffer` directly or synthesizes an arbitrary `size_t length` for it.","H0 parser targets pass `Data, Size`, while `fuzz_ondemand.cpp` constructs `simdjson::padded_string` from a string view backed by the actual fuzz input; these paths constrain lengths to available input size."],"recommended_action":"Add a focused target that consumes fuzz bytes as a size_t length, calls `simdjson::internal::allocate_padded_buffer`, checks null/non-null behavior around `SIZE_MAX - SIMDJSON_PADDING`, the 1 MiB fuzz-build cutoff, and ordinary sizes, and frees every successful allocation."}
